hether an exemption applies to you before you book an exam.</p><h3>Moving From DHA or MOHAP</h3><p>Apply to DOH for a transfer on TAMM while your current license is still valid. Your DataFlow report is transferred to DOH, which may ask for more verification, and specialist titles also need your residency programme documents. Your Abu Dhabi employer then activates the license. Most transfers take 4 to 6 weeks. See <a href=\"https://alphahmc.com/services/healthcare-professional-license-transfer\">license transfers between authorities</a>.</p><h3>Activating and Keeping Your License</h3><p>Once the department confirms you are eligible for the title, your license becomes active when a licensed facility in Abu Dhabi employs you and <a href=\"https://alphahmc.com/services/activate-your-uae-healthcare-license\">activates it</a>. Every year you complete continuing education in your specialty: 40 CME credits for physicians and dentists, 20 for nurses and pharmacists, and 10 for allied health professionals. Surgical specialists also submit a logbook every two years for renewal.</p><h3>Avoiding Delays</h3><ul><li>Get a recent good standing certificate. It must come from the regulator where you last practised and be no more than six months old when you apply.</li><li>Check your time out of practice. After more than three years, the PQR requires CME credits and a training period in an approved setting. Non-UAE nationals cannot apply after more than five years away.</li><li>Use an exemption while it applies. No exemption applies after more than two years out of practice.</li></ul><p>The license is issued by the <a href=\"https://www.doh.gov.ae\">Department of Health Abu Dhabi</a>; a DHA or MOHAP license does not cover Abu Dhabi. Not sure which authority applies to you? <a href=\"https://alphahmc.com/service-packages/healthcare-professional-licensing-uae\">Compare DHA, DOH and MOHAP</a>.</p>",
